 "title": "Act like the person you want to become",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator advises that to change your life, you must start behaving like your future self before life gives you proof. Instead of waiting until you are successful to feel confident, you should act as if you already belong and are used to your success.",
 "key_points": [
  "If you want your life to change, start behaving like it already has.",
  "When walking into a room where you feel you do not belong, act like you have been there before.",
  "Do not shrink yourself around people who are more successful than you.",
  "When something you have been wanting finally happens, do not act shocked; act like you are used to it.",
  "Do not wait to become successful to act confident.",
  "Start becoming familiar with the person you are trying to be before life gives you proof that you are them.",
  "Walk into the room like you belong there and take opportunities like you expected them.",
  "Let good things happen without immediately wondering when they are going to disappear.",
  "You are not pretending to be someone else, you are rehearsing a version of yourself that already exists within you."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by unfilterxd22. Text / caption: fake it till you make it is a PRINCIPLE. Transcript: Look, it's this simple. If you want your life to change, you have to start behaving like it already has. The next time you walk into a room where you feel like you don't belong, act like you've been there before. Or the next time you're around people more successful than you, don't shrink yourself. The next time something you've been wanting finally happens, don't act shocked. Just act like you're used to it. Because you can't keep telling yourself, oh, I'll act confident when I actually become successful. That's backwards. You have to start becoming familiar with the person you're trying to be before life gives you proof that you are them. So walk into the room like you belong there. Take that opportunity like you expected it. Let good things happen without immediately wondering when they're going to disappear. You're not pretending to be someone else. You're rehearsing a version of yourself that already exists within you. Just start acting like it. Text on screen: Look, it's this simple, If you want your life to change, you have to start behaving like it already has, The next time you walk into a room where you feel like you don't belong act like you've been there before, or the next time you're around people more successful than you, don't shrink yourself, The next time something you've been wanting finally happens, don't act shocked, Just act like you're used to it, because you can't keep telling yourself, oh, I'll act confident when I actually become successful, That's backwards, You have to start becoming familiar with the person you're trying to be, Before life gives you proof that you are them, So walk into the room like you belong there, Take that opportunity like you expected it, Let good things happen without immediately wondering when they're going to disappear, You're not pretending to be someone else, You're rehearsing a version of you